#DESCRIPTION
2D hybrid free-stream through a fixed-field/inflow-particle face: no Bx layer

Regression test for spurious Bx growth next to a Dirichlet (fixed field +
inflow particle) upstream face. The setup is the upstream state and the +x boundary of a 2D perpendicular
shock deck, without the reflecting wall: a uniform plasma flows along -x
(n = 5 /cc, ux = -1163 km/s, T = 6.28e5 K) across B = (0, By, 0) with the
motional field E = -u x B. The +x face injects the flow (fixed field +
inflow particles, the shock-deck upstream boundary); the -x face is open.
Hall term, warm adiabatic electrons (Te = 141 eV) and the default upwind
dissipation are on, as in the shock decks.

A uniform flow must stay uniform, so Bx stays at the PIC noise level
everywhere. Two boundary bugs made Bx grow in a layer next to the inflow
face (to ~0.09 |B| by t = 10): the hyper-resistive E (which this deck used
before the upwind term) took the prescribed B
instead of its Laplacian at Dirichlet faces, and the last physical cell of
cell-centered B was overwritten with the prescribed state every call.
validate.py checks that Bx next to the inflow face stays at the interior
noise level.

